# Morgan D-CFO Azure App Service Deployment Plan

## Goal

Deploy the validated hardened Morgan TypeScript build to the existing Azure App Service `morganfinanceagent-webapp` in resource group `rg-morgan-finance-agent`, subscription `260948a4-1d5e-42c8-b095-33a6641ad189`, without changing the separate Agent 365 blueprint instance or Microsoft Foundry hosted-container deployment.

## Current target

- Runtime: Node.js 20 on Linux Azure App Service
- State: Running
- Region: Australia East
- Managed identity: System assigned
- Public host: `https://morganfinanceagent-webapp.azurewebsites.net`
- Deployment method: Existing ZIP deployment script, code-only mode

## Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  User[Signed-in finance operator] --> App[Azure App Service\nMorgan Mission Control]
  App --> Files[Durable App Service files\nSingle-instance mission/HITL state]
  App --> AOAI[Azure OpenAI]
  App --> M365[Agent 365 / Microsoft Graph\nwhen configured]
  App --> Monitor[Azure Monitor OpenTelemetry\nwhen configured]
  Policy[Server-side policy + HITL] --> App
```

## Deployment controls

1. Re-run `npm test` and `npm audit --omit=dev` against the exact workspace.
2. Preserve existing App Service settings, EasyAuth configuration, managed-identity roles, and unrelated Azure resources.
3. Add only the new governance settings:
   - Entra approver object ID and tenant
   - Dedicated generated HITL signing secret
   - Durable App Service file paths
   - Explicit finance-operator requirement
   - Demo approval seeding for the isolated showcase
   - Inbound caller default-deny policy
4. Enable HTTPS-only on the existing web app.
5. Deploy with `scripts/deploy-appservice-zip.cjs --skip-settings --skip-auth --skip-roles`.
6. Validate public liveness, authenticated sign-in behavior, Mission Control, Trust Center, approval queue, and application logs.
7. Preserve the generated ZIP path for rollback investigation. Do not modify the Agent 365 blueprint instance or Foundry hosted agent.

## Security notes

- No secret values are printed or committed.
- The signing secret is generated in memory and stored as an App Service setting for this showcase deployment; Key Vault is the recommended next production step.
- File-backed approvals and scheduler leases are explicitly single-instance controls. Cosmos transactional storage is still required before horizontal scaling.
- Deterministic Contoso and Microsoft IQ data remains visibly labelled as demo data.
